{"explanation":"The sine graph is wavy because sine comes from going around a circle. Picture a point moving around a circle of radius 1. At angle θ, sin θ is just the point's height. As it goes around, it rises to the top (height 1), drops back through the middle (0), sinks to the bottom (−1), and climbs back again. If you plot that height against the angle, you get a smooth wave. The wave repeats every 2π because every full turn brings the point back to where it started. In the animation, turn on "Auto spin" or drag the angle slider. The green height on the circle traces out the blue curve.","manimCode":"const R = 1.5;
const cx = -4.5, cy = 0;

const ax = new Axes({
  xRange: [0, 2 * Math.PI, Math.PI / 2],
  yRange: [-1.5, 1.5, 0.5],
  xLength: 7, yLength: 4.5, tips: false
});
ax.moveTo([2, 0, 0]);

const circle = new Circle({ radius: R, color: GRAY });
circle.moveTo([cx, cy, 0]);
const centerDot = new Dot({ point: [cx, cy, 0], color: GRAY });

const radiusLine = new Polygon({ vertices: [[cx, cy, 0], [cx + R, cy, 0]], color: WHITE });
radiusLine.setStrokeWidth(3).setFillOpacity(0);
const heightLine = new Polygon({ vertices: [[cx + R, cy, 0], [cx + R, cy, 0]], color: GREEN });
heightLine.setStrokeWidth(5).setFillOpacity(0);
const connector = new Polygon({ vertices: [[cx + R, cy, 0], [cx + R, cy, 0]], color: YELLOW });
connector.setStrokeWidth(1.5).setFillOpacity(0);
const graphHeight = new Polygon({ vertices: [ax.c2p(0, 0), ax.c2p(0, 0)], color: GREEN });
graphHeight.setStrokeWidth(4).setFillOpacity(0);

const circDot = new Dot({ point: [cx + R, cy, 0], color: YELLOW });
const graphDot = new Dot({ point: ax.c2p(0, 0), color: YELLOW });

const ghost = ax.plot(x => Math.sin(x), { color: BLUE_E });
ghost.setOpacity(0.25);

let trace = null;

scene.add(ax, ghost, circle, centerDot, radiusLine, heightLine, connector, graphHeight, circDot, graphDot);

const title = new MathTex({ latex: 'y = \\sin\\theta = \\text{height of the point}', color: WHITE });
await title.waitForRender();
title.scale(0.8);
title.moveTo([0, 3.3, 0]);
scene.add(title);

const thetaLbl = new MathTex({ latex: '\\theta', color: YELLOW });
await thetaLbl.waitForRender();
thetaLbl.moveTo([cx + 0.35, cy + 0.2, 0]);
scene.add(thetaLbl);

let theta = 0;
let auto = true;

function render() {
  const px = cx + R * Math.cos(theta);
  const py = cy + R * Math.sin(theta);
  const gp = ax.c2p(theta, Math.sin(theta));
  circDot.moveTo([px, py, 0]);
  graphDot.moveTo(gp);
  radiusLine.setVertices([[cx, cy, 0], [px, py, 0]]);
  heightLine.setVertices([[px, cy, 0], [px, py, 0]]);
  connector.setVertices([[px, py, 0], gp]);
  graphHeight.setVertices([ax.c2p(theta, 0), gp]);
  if (trace) { scene.remove(trace); trace = null; }
  if (theta > 0.02) {
    trace = ax.plot(x => Math.sin(x), { color: BLUE, xRange: [0, theta] });
    trace.setStrokeWidth(5);
    scene.add(trace);
  }
}

render();

circDot.addUpdater((m, dt) => {
  if (!auto) return;
  const step = (typeof dt === 'number' && dt > 0 && dt < 0.2) ? dt : 1 / 60;
  theta += step * 0.8;
  if (theta > 2 * Math.PI) theta = 0;
  render();
});

const controls = new Controls(scene, { position: 'top-right' });
controls.addCheckbox({ label: 'Auto spin', checked: true, onChange: (c) => { auto = c; } });
controls.addSlider({
  label: 'Angle θ', min: 0, max: 2 * Math.PI, value: 0, step: 0.05,
  onChange: (v) => { auto = false; theta = v; render(); }
});
controls.addButton({ label: 'Reset', onClick: () => { theta = 0; render(); } });

await scene.wait(999999);"}

